          "anchor": "Four nuisance cases and four population targets"
        }
      ],
      "supported_claims": [
        "Correct marginal outcome mean and conditional effect with wrong propensity can yield 3/2 instead of true 2.",
        "Correct propensity or both correctly reconstructed outcome surfaces recover 2 in the stipulated law.",
        "Equal groups with propensities 1/2 and 1/10 and effects -4 and 12 have ATE 4, ATT -4/3, ATC 44/7 and overlap effect 4/17.",
        "Assumed cost 2 gives customer-population margin 2 and overlap-population margin -30/17."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Exact hypothetical laws with fixed nuisance values; no fitted forest or simulation.",
        "The bias identity is conditional on fixed nuisance functions and a fresh observation.",
        "Algebra does not establish finite-sample coverage or validate a data-dependent selected cohort.",
        "Dollar effects and costs are assumptions, not observed bank returns."
      ]
    }
